    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Saying no without saying «no»",
     "texto": [
      "A common way to decline indirectly is **ちょっと…** (well, the thing is… a bit…) and to leave the sentence unfinished. It usually suggests a refusal, although its meaning depends on the situation, the relationship and the tone. A direct refusal can also be appropriate when clarity is needed.",
      "**また こんど** = another time."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
